a1=(1,1);
b1=(0,1);
c1=(0.5,1.6);
d1=(1,0);

draw(a1--b1--c1--a1);
draw(a1--d1--b1);
draw(d1--c1);

label("$A$",d1,SW);
label("$B$",c1,NE);

[/asy]

A bag contains $2$ white balls and $n(n\geqslant 2,n\in\mathbb{N}^{*})$ red balls. Each time, two balls are drawn from the bag (and then replaced back into the bag). If the two balls drawn have the same color, it is considered a win; otherwise, it is a loss.
(I) Express the probability of winning in one draw using an algebraic formula containing $n$;
(II) If $n=3$, find the probability of winning exactly once in three draws;
(III) Let $f(p)$ be the probability of winning exactly once in three draws. Find the value of $n$ when $f(p)$ reaches its maximum.

Given an ellipse $C$: $\dfrac{y^2}{a^2}+\dfrac{x^2}{b^2}=1$ ($a > b > 0$) with eccentricity $\dfrac{1}{2}$, and its upper focus point is $F(0,1)$. A moving line $l$ passing through $F$ intersects the ellipse $C$ at points $M$ and $N$. Let point $P(3,4)$, and denote the slopes of $PM$ and $PN$ as $k_1$ and $k_2$, respectively.

(Ⅰ) Find the equation of the ellipse $C$;

(Ⅱ) If the slope of line $l$ is $-1$, find the value of $k_1·k_2$;

(Ⅲ) Investigate whether $\dfrac{1}{k_1}+\dfrac{1}{k_2}$ is a constant value? If yes, find this constant value; if not, find the range of $\dfrac{1}{k_1}+\dfrac{1}{k_2}$.

In triangle $\triangle ABC$, $\tan B = \frac{4}{3}$. Given that $AB = 3$ units, find the length of side $BC$.

