1's common left and right vertices, $P$ and $Q$ are moving points on the hyperbola and ellipse, respectively, different from $A$ and $B$, and satisfy: $\overrightarrow{A P}+\overrightarrow{B P}=\lambda(\widehat{A Q}+\overrightarrow{B Q})(\lambda \in \mathbf{R}$ and $|\lambda|>1)$. Let the slopes of the lines $A P$, $B P$, $A Q$, and $B Q$ be $k_{1}$, $k_{2}$, $k_{3}$, and $k_{4}$, respectively.
